Description: Use ntohl() for the 32-bit v3+ packet buffer_length field
 validate_request() read the network-order buffer_length of v3/v4
 packets with ntohs(), truncating the value to 16 bits. For every
 request with a buffer smaller than 65536 bytes the computed index was
 0, so the forced string termination was written to buffer[-1] instead
 of the end of the buffer, and the buffer was never terminated at the
 declared length. The field is 32 bits wide and must use ntohl().
Origin: vendor
Forwarded: https://github.com/NagiosEnterprises/nrpe/issues
---
--- a/src/nrpe.c	2026-10-02 22:54:59.604278211 +0200
+++ b/src/nrpe.c	2026-10-03 00:07:45.600965769 +0200
@@ -2620,7 +2620,7 @@
 
 	/* make sure buffer is terminated */
 	if (packet_ver >= NRPE_PACKET_VERSION_3) {
-		int32_t   l = ntohs(v3pkt->buffer_length);
+		int32_t   l = ntohl(v3pkt->buffer_length);
 		v3pkt->buffer[l - 1] = '\x0';
 		buff = v3pkt->buffer;
 	} else {
